language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ among: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Find an array x of n integers between 0 and 7, inclusive, such that exactly m of them take one of the values in v. The other elements may take any other value in that range.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `among.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/among.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `among_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py among.json
$   savilerow model.eprime among_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the length of the array x
given n : int(1..)
$ m: the exact number of entries of x that must take a value listed in v
given m : int(0..)
$ v_dim1: the number of values in v, derived from the data (the length of v; not a field of the reader's JSON)
given v_dim1 : int(1..)
$ v[k]: the k-th value of the set v, indices 1-based
given v : matrix indexed by [int(1..v_dim1)] of int

$ x[i]: the i-th element of the array, indices 1-based, with values from 0 to 7
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..7)
$ inset[i]: element x[i] takes one of the values listed in v (auxiliary)
find inset : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool

branching on [x]

such that
$ inset[i] holds exactly when x[i] equals one of the values in v
forAll i : int(1..n) . (inset[i] <-> (exists k : int(1..v_dim1) . x[i] = v[k])),
$ exactly m elements of x take one of the values in v
(sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(inset[i])) = m
